<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aedui</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Haedui</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aedui or Haedui were a Gallic people of central-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, living between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saone">Saône</a> in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> and the Roman period. Their civitas was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oligarchy">oligarchy</a> run by a senate and an annual magistrate, the vergobret. From the middle of the 2nd century BCE they were allies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, the first people of inner Gaul to make a formal treaty with the Republic. They gave Caesar uneven support in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallic-wars">Gallic Wars</a> before briefly joining the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a> in 52 BCE. In 48 CE they became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauls">Gauls</a> admitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-senate">Roman Senate</a>, and their capital moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bibracte">Bibracte</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/autun">Augustodunum</a> (Autun).</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aedui.jpg" alt="Aedui" width="330" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eugène Hucher (1814-1889) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dumnorix_monnaie_d'argent_15mm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
